Racer: credits

Everything in this game was made for it: code, the karts, the props and eight
worlds, the procedural textures, the colour grades and the synthesized sound
and music (tools/make-audio.mjs, tools/make-music.mjs, and battle mode's pop and
knockout from tools/make-battle-audio.mjs). The exceptions are the fonts, the
announcer's voice and the realistic maps' ground textures, trees, grass and rocks
below.

Fonts (from github.com/google/fonts; each licence ships beside its font in
assets/fonts/):

  Bungee (Regular): titles, the position and the clock.
    Copyright 2023 The Bungee Project Authors (https://github.com/djrrb/Bungee).
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/Bungee-OFL.txt).

  Fredoka (Bold): menus and HUD text.
    Copyright 2016 The Fredoka Project Authors.
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/Fredoka-OFL.txt).

  Oswald (variable): small print.
    Copyright 2016 The Oswald Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/OswaldFont).
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/Oswald-OFL.txt).

The announcer (assets/audio/voice/, 110 Ogg files): the lines were written for
the game and spoken by a text-to-speech model run locally by
tools/make-voice.mjs, which then gives them their stadium sound (its own
filters, compressor, limiter, echoes and reverb). Nothing was recorded.

  Kokoro-82M v1.0, voice am_fenrir: the speech model and its voice pack.
    Copyright hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M).
    Apache License 2.0. Run from its ONNX build,
    onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX (Apache License 2.0).

  kokoro-js 1.2.1 (https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro, Apache License 2.0)
  with Transformers.js 3.8.1 (Hugging Face, Apache License 2.0) and
  onnxruntime-node 1.21.0 (Microsoft, MIT): the runner. Tools only; none of their code ships.

  phonemizer 1.2.1 (npm, Apache License 2.0; eSpeak NG compiled to
  WebAssembly, GPL-3.0): turns the words into phonemes for the model. A tool
  only; none of its code ships.

  Whisper base.en (OpenAI, MIT), run with Transformers.js: make-voice.mjs
  --asr transcribes every file back to check that it says its words. A check
  only; nothing of it ships.

